    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37738" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-mĭco</span></b> , āre,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to gleam</i> or <i>glitter forth</i>,
				<i>to glitter very much</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lucerna claro lumine praemicans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 167, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praemicantis lunae candor nimius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11</span></i>
			, p. 257 <i>init.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">galea nitore praemicans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10</span></i>
			, p. 238; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 1,
		84.</div>
